notes: >-
  The Aura license is all rights reserved with a research-use grant — see
  LICENSE in the source tree. The grant lets anyone run the code to
  reproduce, verify, or test the results of the paper named in
  preferred-citation, and publish what they find with a citation. Citation
  does not confer copying, redistribution, modification, or derivative-work
  rights, and no patent license is granted. Quantitative claims
  should cite the proof bundle artifacts generated by `make proof-bundle`,
  especially CAA_32B_RESULTS.json and STDP_EXTERNAL_VALIDATION.json.

  The release that paper reports is tagged isc-preprint-2026-11 and archived
  on Zenodo. Otherwise cite a commit rather than a version: the `version`
  field in pyproject.toml reads 2026.4.20 and has not tracked the work, which
  CHANGELOG.md records under "Known version drift".

  The ten theories are the ones TheoryArbitrationFramework registers — GWT,
  IIT 4.0, predictive coding, recurrent processing, higher-order thought,
  multiple drafts, attention schema, free energy, enactivism, illusionism —
  each with a role and a module, in core/consciousness/theory_arbitration.py.
